1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:04,738
‪PREVIOUSLY ON ‪CHOSEN HOME

2
00:00:04,804 --> 00:00:06,539
Genichi Hatano, a man afraid of love

3
00:00:06,606 --> 00:00:08,541
after a comment made
by a marriage agency staff

4
00:00:08,608 --> 00:00:09,576
begins to change.

5
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:11,678
Love and revolution.

6
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:14,714
His love interest, Saku Sakuta,
is a middle school teacher.

7
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:15,915
Saku’s student,

8
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:18,151
Hotaru Kusunoki,
shows up carrying 30 million yen.

9
00:00:18,218 --> 00:00:19,719
Party A’s mother, Tomoe Kusunoki,

10
00:00:19,786 --> 00:00:22,555
is wanted for embezzlement
from her company and is on the run.

11
00:00:22,622 --> 00:00:24,891
- Not wanting to see Hotaru suffer,
- Please.

12
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:27,394
Genichi decides to pose as her father.
But…

13
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:28,595
I'm Jin Ichigaya.

14
00:00:28,661 --> 00:00:30,630
Your stage name is Genichi Hatano?

15
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:33,299
…to the police,
he tells a lie far too big to sustain.

16
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,668
- Hey.
- That lie is then

17
00:00:35,735 --> 00:00:37,837
exposed instantly
when Hotaru's real dad appears.

18
00:00:37,904 --> 00:00:39,305
You’ve been lying all this time?

19
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:41,041
And finally, a confession.

20
00:00:41,107 --> 00:00:42,409
I like you.

21
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:43,910
Meanwhile, Hotaru’s mom

22
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:46,980
continues her runaway journey,
wandering across Japan.

23
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:48,948
I won’t be coming home for a while.

24
00:00:49,015 --> 00:00:50,917
- I'll be back.
- Excuse me!

25
00:00:50,984 --> 00:00:51,885
Yes?

26
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:54,888
TAMOTSU’S LITTLE GIFT SHOP

27
00:00:54,954 --> 00:00:56,189
The day before yesterday,

28
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:57,690
or maybe the day before that,

29
00:00:57,757 --> 00:01:00,460
I think, I sent a letter to Tokyo.

30
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:02,495
- Right.
- Has it arrived by any chance?

31
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:04,130
Did you send it out by mistake, perhaps?

32
00:01:05,665 --> 00:01:06,566
Why do you ask?

33
00:01:06,633 --> 00:01:07,801
You sound like you wished
it wasn't sent out.

34
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:11,037
Ah, no…

35
00:01:11,104 --> 00:01:12,572
I’m not sure.

36
00:01:13,473 --> 00:01:14,841
Maybe I did send it to the wrong place.

37
00:01:17,143 --> 00:01:19,479
I honestly don’t know myself too.

38
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:24,884
I said…

39
00:01:26,953 --> 00:01:27,921
I like you!

40
00:01:27,987 --> 00:01:28,988
Huh?

41
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:30,790
Because I like you.

42
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,225
Saying to use a house as a "clamp"

43
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:34,194
and accompanying you to the viewing…

44
00:01:34,961 --> 00:01:37,197
I did those things…

45
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,531
because…

46
00:01:39,666 --> 00:01:40,500
I like you.

47
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:43,303
But more importantly…!

48
00:01:43,369 --> 00:01:44,370
What's more important?

49
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,673
We’re talking about Hotaru.

50
00:01:46,739 --> 00:01:47,874
If exposed, you’ll be arrested.

51
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:48,875
Right.

52
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:52,011
What if her biological dad
decides to report you?

53
00:01:52,078 --> 00:01:53,012
That’d be bad.

54
00:01:53,646 --> 00:01:56,416
You even lied to the police.

55
00:01:57,016 --> 00:01:59,452
You told Ms. Matsu
your name was Jin Ichigaya.

56
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:02,255
That "Genichi Hatano" was a stage name
when you were aiming to be

57
00:02:02,322 --> 00:02:03,156
a musician and stuff.

58
00:02:03,223 --> 00:02:04,891
- That part is true.
- What?

59
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:07,026
I did aim to be a musician.

60
00:02:07,093 --> 00:02:09,128
That's beside the point!

61
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:12,298
Using a fake name is the real problem, no?

62
00:02:12,365 --> 00:02:14,200
Pull yourself together!

63
00:02:14,701 --> 00:02:16,402
Are you still going to act as her parent?

64
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:17,937
I already signed the contract.

65
00:02:18,004 --> 00:02:19,772
Come on…

66
00:02:19,839 --> 00:02:22,041
What’s this? A strategy meeting?

67
00:02:22,542 --> 00:02:24,711
‪-Got you!
‪-Something like that.

68
00:02:24,777 --> 00:02:26,713
No, it’s not!

69
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:29,382
He's definitely gonna show up again.

70
00:02:29,449 --> 00:02:31,718
- I’ll keep an eye out too.
- You're fine with this?

71
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:33,253
- Huh?
- You're his accomplice then.

72
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:34,287
You know…

73
00:02:34,787 --> 00:02:36,589
That's actually kinda cool!

74
00:02:37,524 --> 00:02:39,025
What? Come on!

75
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:41,494
- Okay.
- Your hand.

76
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:43,463
For Hotaru’s sake,

77
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,732
we’re in this together!

78
00:02:45,798 --> 00:02:47,167
Y-Yeah…

79
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:49,235
You need to be more enthusiastic!

80
00:02:49,802 --> 00:02:50,870
- One more time.
- Okay.

81
00:02:50,937 --> 00:02:53,072
- For Hotaru’s sake,
- For Hotaru’s sake,

82
00:02:53,139 --> 00:02:55,542
- let's do this together!
- let's do this together.

83
00:02:55,608 --> 00:02:56,776
That’s different from just now.

84
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,711
‪-"Let’s do this together."
‪-Again?

85
00:02:58,778 --> 00:03:01,214
‪-Say, "Let’s do this together."
‪-Yes, "Let’s do this together."

86
00:03:01,281 --> 00:03:02,115
TO HOTARU KUSUNOKI

87
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:03,249
Let's do this together… Got it.

88
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:06,619
Let's do this together!

89
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,889
- One last time. Now, hold this.
- This?

90
00:03:09,956 --> 00:03:11,891
- Give it your all.
- Yes.

91
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:14,661
Let's do this together!

92
00:03:18,798 --> 00:03:20,400
Wait for me!

93
00:03:26,606 --> 00:03:28,508
MAY I ASK A QUESTION?

94
00:03:28,575 --> 00:03:31,544
IF A COMPLETE STRANGER PRETENDS TO BE
A MINOR’S PARENT, IS THAT A CRIME?

95
00:03:31,611 --> 00:03:32,445
IN SOME CASES, THIS MAY BE CONSIDERED
A CRIMINAL OFFENSE

96
00:03:32,512 --> 00:03:33,346
YOU MAY BE CHARGED WITH FORGERY
VIOLATION OF THE CHILD WELFARE ACT

97
00:03:33,413 --> 00:03:34,380
YOUTH PROTECTION LAWS
THE MINOR OFFENSES ACT, ETC.

98
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:35,848
POSSIBLE APPLICABLE OFFENSES ARE…

99
00:03:38,451 --> 00:03:39,619
Mr. Sakuta.

100
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:40,753
One moment, please.

101
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:41,721
Yes?

102
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,525
What's the matter?

103
00:03:45,592 --> 00:03:47,393
That man’s been loitering around,
hasn’t he?

104
00:03:52,098 --> 00:03:53,533
Why are you here today?

105
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,102
THIS IS THE REAR GATE. PLEASE USE
MAIN ENTRANCE. NO UNAUTHORIZED VEHICLES

106
00:03:56,169 --> 00:03:58,705
To see my daughter. Is there an issue?

107
00:03:58,771 --> 00:04:01,174
Is this about the money?

108
00:04:02,275 --> 00:04:03,843
She's definitely hiding it.

109
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:07,280
There’s no way my ex-wife
would embezzle money just for herself.

110
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:08,748
She’s too much of a coward.

111
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,550
If she really did it,

112
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:12,318
then it had to be for Hotaru.

113
00:04:12,819 --> 00:04:14,854
So, do you know anything about it?

114
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,256
No.

115
00:04:17,657 --> 00:04:20,059
What about that man, then?

116
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,630
The fool that's calling himself her dad.

117
00:04:24,631 --> 00:04:26,699
I found out on that day too

118
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:28,301
that he’s not really her dad.

119
00:04:35,575 --> 00:04:36,609
Could it be

120
00:04:37,343 --> 00:04:38,745
you swing that way too?

121
00:04:40,513 --> 00:04:42,882
That guy is gay, right?

122
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:45,218
So, I thought maybe
you're in on it with him.

123
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:48,054
Are you going to report him then?

124
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:50,823
No way.

125
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:53,326
If he gets arrested,

126
00:04:53,826 --> 00:04:55,895
I have to take care of Hotaru then.

127
00:04:56,396 --> 00:04:57,563
Never in hell.

128
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,434
So, you really…

129
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,270
All you really care about
is the money, huh?

130
00:05:04,904 --> 00:05:06,439
What else could there be?

131
00:05:06,506 --> 00:05:08,374
Then could you please stop coming here?

132
00:05:08,441 --> 00:05:10,443
Oh, come on. I'm her dad.

133
00:05:11,010 --> 00:05:12,545
She didn’t come to school today.

134
00:05:13,112 --> 00:05:14,147
Please leave.

135
00:05:20,053 --> 00:05:21,054
Thank you!

136
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,088
PARFAIT

137
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:32,532
- Mr. Hatano!
- Hello.

138
00:05:32,598 --> 00:05:33,666
THE SETTING SUN

139
00:05:33,733 --> 00:05:35,435
I love the parfaits here.

140
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:36,803
I come every now and then.

141
00:05:36,869 --> 00:05:37,937
SHOPS & REST HOUSE FOOD

142
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,005
Me too.

143
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,307
It’s a treat to myself for doing well.

144
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:44,677
Um, what's that?

145
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,683
"Love and revolution"…

146
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,452
I was wondering what it meant.

147
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:55,755
The other day, I just randomly quoted

148
00:05:56,489 --> 00:05:58,324
from 10 Quotes That Touch Your Heart.

149
00:05:58,391 --> 00:06:00,526
It's a short video I came across,

150
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:01,994
and I just said it to you as-is.

151
00:06:02,595 --> 00:06:03,429
I see now.

152
00:06:03,496 --> 00:06:06,632
At work, I tend to say things
just to look cool.

153
00:06:08,167 --> 00:06:09,402
Sorry about that.

154
00:06:10,136 --> 00:06:11,270
Don't worry about it.

155
00:06:11,771 --> 00:06:13,272
- That's why you're reading that?
- Yes.

156
00:06:13,339 --> 00:06:14,574
For my own learning.

157
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,808
Right.

158
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,677
Have you not read it?

159
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,680
I did a long time ago.

160
00:06:21,647 --> 00:06:22,749
What was it about again?

161
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,353
To put it simply,
it’s like fighting old morals.

162
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:30,890
I get how the characters feel,

163
00:06:30,957 --> 00:06:32,558
but their actions make no sense.

164
00:06:32,625 --> 00:06:35,128
The heroine's "love and revolution"
basically means

165
00:06:35,194 --> 00:06:37,597
having a child with a married man

166
00:06:37,663 --> 00:06:39,532
and raising it herself.

167
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,034
That’d make headlines these days.

168
00:06:42,101 --> 00:06:43,536
Right?

169
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:46,873
But…

170
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,742
maybe that's just how things
are meant to be.

171
00:06:49,809 --> 00:06:53,045
Everyone has their own
"love and revolution", I guess?

172
00:06:54,313 --> 00:06:55,448
Really?

173
00:06:56,816 --> 00:06:59,819
How’s your "love and revolution" going,
Mr. Hatano? Any progress?

174
00:07:00,453 --> 00:07:03,489
- I guess so?
- What?

175
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:04,657
I confessed my love.

176
00:07:04,724 --> 00:07:05,658
Really?

177
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:10,563
He doesn’t seem
all that interested, though.

178
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:13,099
Then make him interested.

179
00:07:13,166 --> 00:07:14,200
How?

180
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,002
Convince him it’s fate.

181
00:07:18,371 --> 00:07:21,641
We met at the agency,
then again at the park?

182
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:24,243
That's all fate, right?

183
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,312
Wait, both of us?

184
00:07:27,013 --> 00:07:28,114
Something like that!

185
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:30,650
- Right.
- Yeah.

186
00:07:34,187 --> 00:07:36,489
Is that also some kind of quote
or something?

187
00:07:36,556 --> 00:07:37,390
Oh, no.

188
00:07:38,391 --> 00:07:41,093
This is from a book called
100 Foolproof Love Techniques.

189
00:07:43,196 --> 00:07:45,264
Don’t you think
the number of fences increased?

190
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:47,433
Did it?

191
00:07:48,734 --> 00:07:50,603
It used to only go this far.

192
00:07:51,671 --> 00:07:53,406
Now that you mention it…

193
00:07:53,906 --> 00:07:55,174
What if they keep adding more,

194
00:07:55,241 --> 00:07:57,376
and there's nowhere left for us to go?

195
00:07:57,443 --> 00:07:58,711
Even fill the roads with fences?

196
00:07:59,212 --> 00:08:00,713
Like all over the place.

197
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,114
What do we do if we're surrounded?

198
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,684
Coming.

199
00:08:05,952 --> 00:08:07,320
- What's wrong?
- Just for a bit.

200
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:10,056
Could it be your dad came again?

201
00:08:10,122 --> 00:08:12,391
Nope, he didn't.

202
00:08:12,458 --> 00:08:13,926
Then you must be hungry.

203
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:15,328
Oh, before I forget.

204
00:08:19,232 --> 00:08:21,167
Here. A spare key.

205
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:23,703
Just in case your dad shows up again.

206
00:08:24,403 --> 00:08:25,705
Or, you know,

207
00:08:25,771 --> 00:08:26,839
if you ever get hungry,

208
00:08:26,906 --> 00:08:29,275
feel free to grab anything
from the fridge.

209
00:08:33,813 --> 00:08:34,780
Then…

210
00:08:35,481 --> 00:08:37,683
I’ll water the plants in return.

211
00:08:38,818 --> 00:08:39,719
Thank you.

212
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,893
Did Mr. Sakuta agree to help too?

213
00:08:46,959 --> 00:08:47,793
What?

214
00:08:48,294 --> 00:08:50,096
You two talked about it yesterday, right?

215
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:52,698
I didn’t say it outright,

216
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:56,135
but I feel like Sakuta would understand.

217
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:00,540
It's easier for me
if I think positively anyway.

218
00:09:01,841 --> 00:09:03,876
- Thinking positively, you say?
- Yeah.

219
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:08,581
I’m starting the laundry first,

220
00:09:08,648 --> 00:09:10,483
so you'd have to wait
before dinner is ready.

221
00:09:11,517 --> 00:09:12,351
Okay.

222
00:09:26,866 --> 00:09:27,700
Yes?

223
00:09:28,935 --> 00:09:32,138
Now? I'm doing laundry…

224
00:09:32,972 --> 00:09:33,806
Sorry about this.

225
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,275
No, it's fine.

226
00:09:36,342 --> 00:09:38,277
Did her dad come by again, by any chance?

227
00:09:38,344 --> 00:09:39,845
No.

228
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:42,214
He came to the school today.

229
00:09:42,281 --> 00:09:44,116
What happened then?

230
00:09:44,183 --> 00:09:47,386
- I told him Hotaru was absent and he left.
- Okay.

231
00:09:47,453 --> 00:09:49,622
She's his daughter, and yet that guy

232
00:09:50,122 --> 00:09:52,291
really doesn’t seem to care about her.

233
00:09:53,726 --> 00:09:55,728
If I were Hotaru, I’d probably
just, you know,

234
00:09:55,795 --> 00:09:57,930
hate everything.

235
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:00,132
Her mom’s gone somewhere,

236
00:10:00,199 --> 00:10:01,901
and her dad’s like that.

237
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:03,703
But…

238
00:10:04,203 --> 00:10:06,739
when I was deceived into thinking
you were her dad…

239
00:10:06,806 --> 00:10:08,641
Sorry about that.

240
00:10:08,708 --> 00:10:10,076
To be frank,

241
00:10:10,142 --> 00:10:12,511
I did feel you were unreliable.

242
00:10:13,012 --> 00:10:14,313
Still, I was glad.

243
00:10:15,181 --> 00:10:18,084
That she had a dad
who was trying his best.

244
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:20,052
I was really happy for her.

245
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:23,389
So… Well, it may be wrong.

246
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,257
No, it's wrong on all levels.

247
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:28,194
But for the effort she's putting in,

248
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,129
I'd like to respect it.

249
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:31,731
Does that mean…

250
00:10:32,231 --> 00:10:33,966
I support you
in pretending to be her parent.

251
00:10:36,035 --> 00:10:37,236
Are you sure that's okay?

252
00:10:38,437 --> 00:10:40,973
- What?
- I mean, you're a teacher.

253
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:42,441
If this gets exposed,

254
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:44,777
wouldn't you be forced to resign?

255
00:10:45,878 --> 00:10:47,380
Well…

256
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:49,382
I'm fine with that.

257
00:10:49,949 --> 00:10:51,851
I don't even like school to begin with.

258
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,286
And yet you became a teacher?

259
00:10:54,353 --> 00:10:56,756
I wanted to be a teacher
who doesn’t like school.

260
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:57,790
Wow.

261
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,993
It's weird, right?

262
00:11:02,028 --> 00:11:04,230
No, being who you want to be

263
00:11:04,296 --> 00:11:05,131
is impressive.

264
00:11:07,066 --> 00:11:09,568
I hated school too.

265
00:11:09,635 --> 00:11:10,503
Hold up.

266
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,675
- Isn’t this fate?
- Huh?

267
00:11:16,575 --> 00:11:17,810
Fate.

268
00:11:18,310 --> 00:11:19,845
- What is?
- Never mind.

269
00:11:20,379 --> 00:11:22,481
It's nothing. Sorry.

270
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:26,318
Anyway, the next strategy meeting.

271
00:11:26,385 --> 00:11:27,386
I'll be there.

272
00:11:27,453 --> 00:11:28,320
Okay.

273
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,324
Sorry to keep you waiting.

274
00:11:35,728 --> 00:11:36,729
What's wrong?

275
00:11:57,083 --> 00:11:59,151
- Hey. Get in.
- What do you want?

276
00:11:59,819 --> 00:12:00,720
- Don't touch me.
- Huh?

277
00:12:00,786 --> 00:12:02,388
Sit tight.

278
00:12:03,422 --> 00:12:06,058
Wait, what? Huh?

279
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:08,928
What in the world?!

280
00:12:10,496 --> 00:12:13,566
- It's a kidnapping! Call the police!
- Kidnapping?

281
00:12:13,632 --> 00:12:15,367
But it's her biological dad.

282
00:12:15,434 --> 00:12:16,702
Even if we call the police…

283
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:18,437
I-Is that so?

284
00:12:18,504 --> 00:12:20,506
I'm not sure.

285
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:23,776
What's that?

286
00:12:23,843 --> 00:12:25,077
A letter?

287
00:12:25,611 --> 00:12:27,413
- From Hotaru?
- Did she run away from home?

288
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,581
"To Hotaru.

289
00:12:28,647 --> 00:12:30,583
Let's meet at Lakeside Café.

290
00:12:30,649 --> 00:12:31,650
Make sure

291
00:12:31,717 --> 00:12:33,819
to bring the money with you.

292
00:12:34,453 --> 00:12:35,354
From Tomoe Kusunoki."

293
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:37,790
That's Hotaru's mom.

294
00:12:37,857 --> 00:12:39,592
Is it really her, though?

295
00:12:40,993 --> 00:12:42,695
Asking her to bring the money?

296
00:12:43,295 --> 00:12:44,597
It could be the work of her dad.

297
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:46,866
If that's the case,
then it's unforgivable!

298
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:49,001
Hotaru thinks it's her mom, right?

299
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:51,270
But I feel like she’d be able
to see through it.

300
00:12:51,337 --> 00:12:52,671
Ah, on the back.

301
00:12:52,738 --> 00:12:53,506
FROM HOTARU KUSUNOKI

302
00:12:55,307 --> 00:12:57,710
"So, I'll be taking the suitcase back.

303
00:12:58,677 --> 00:12:59,845
From Hotaru Kusunoki."

304
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,514
Sorry, make way.

305
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:08,420
It's gone…

306
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:13,993
I can go on my own.

307
00:13:14,059 --> 00:13:16,428
It's okay. I'll take you there.

308
00:13:16,495 --> 00:13:17,997
To Lakeside Café.

309
00:13:18,063 --> 00:13:19,331
How did you know about it?

310
00:13:19,398 --> 00:13:20,933
I checked your mailbox.

311
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,869
If she were to contact anyone,
it'd be you.

312
00:13:25,404 --> 00:13:26,939
I went ahead and read it.

313
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:29,408
So, you did have the money
with you all along.

314
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,446
MR. SAKUTA

315
00:14:30,069 --> 00:14:31,136
Oh, uh…

316
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,838
- Sorry!
- No, I'm sorry!

317
00:14:32,905 --> 00:14:34,440
I'm really sorry about this!

318
00:14:34,506 --> 00:14:36,976
- Wait, I thought this place was…
- I'm sorry!

319
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:38,510
- Sorry.
- I'm really sorry!

320
00:14:38,577 --> 00:14:40,746
- What's wrong?
- I'm so sorry!

321
00:14:41,614 --> 00:14:44,583
If you just want the money,
why not just grab this and scram?

322
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,385
After I drop you off.

323
00:14:46,452 --> 00:14:47,853
Do you want to see Mom?

324
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:49,889
Of course not.

325
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,390
Aren't you doing this for the money?

326
00:14:51,457 --> 00:14:54,660
- I am.
- Then I don't get this entire situation.

327
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:57,496
They don't have a car, right?

328
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,765
- Who, Mom?
- No.

329
00:15:00,966 --> 00:15:01,834
My current dad?

330
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:06,272
Since you probably haven’t been
out anywhere, you're happy, right?

331
00:15:06,839 --> 00:15:10,042
Back when the three of us
used to go out together.

332
00:15:10,109 --> 00:15:11,777
Here, both of you can share these.

333
00:15:11,844 --> 00:15:12,878
Thank you!

334
00:15:13,445 --> 00:15:15,180
We're not going out on a field trip.

335
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:17,516
Oh, this is nostalgic!

336
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:18,884
My parent's home always had this.

337
00:15:18,951 --> 00:15:21,954
Stuff like this
might disappear eventually.

338
00:15:22,021 --> 00:15:24,857
They stopped selling a lot
of these recently, right?

339
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:25,991
Enjoy it while you can.

340
00:15:26,692 --> 00:15:28,494
Thank you. We'll be off now.

341
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,428
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

342
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:34,133
Have a safe trip!

343
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:35,301
These days,

344
00:15:35,367 --> 00:15:37,369
there’s been a lot of talk
about vacant houses.

345
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:41,407
Our company is actually looking to expand
into that kind of business.

346
00:15:41,473 --> 00:15:43,742
Um, you'll be reporting me
to the police, right?

347
00:15:43,809 --> 00:15:44,643
The police?

348
00:15:45,411 --> 00:15:47,212
Ah, you did trespass.

349
00:15:48,013 --> 00:15:49,415
Well, yeah.

350
00:15:50,215 --> 00:15:51,050
You don’t have a home?

351
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:53,118
It’s complicated.

352
00:15:54,219 --> 00:15:57,256
I'm really, really in a pinch.

353
00:15:57,323 --> 00:16:00,259
Please, I’m begging you…
Just don’t report me.

354
00:16:01,393 --> 00:16:03,562
Oh! I’ll give you this in return.

355
00:16:04,363 --> 00:16:06,231
Take whichever ones you like…

356
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:08,033
Oh, I have oranges too.

357
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,268
And this.

358
00:16:09,768 --> 00:16:12,071
You can take them all if you want.

359
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:12,972
‪Yeah.

360
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,442
Are you perhaps…

361
00:16:18,711 --> 00:16:19,845
a backpacker?

362
00:16:19,912 --> 00:16:20,913
What?

363
00:16:21,547 --> 00:16:24,817
So, you’re using this place
as a sort of lodging, huh?

364
00:16:25,551 --> 00:16:27,686
- Sorry about this.
- So, how was it living here?

365
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:29,955
- What?
- Well…

366
00:16:30,022 --> 00:16:32,358
I'm asking because we’re about
to put it on the market.

367
00:16:32,424 --> 00:16:34,593
Is there anything you liked about it?

368
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:37,596
Hmm…

369
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:38,897
Nothing?

370
00:16:39,398 --> 00:16:40,733
Well…

371
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:45,671
Oh, yes!

372
00:16:48,407 --> 00:16:50,509
You haven’t noticed, right?

373
00:16:51,643 --> 00:16:52,478
Sorry, what?

374
00:16:54,046 --> 00:16:55,047
Never mind.

375
00:16:55,114 --> 00:16:56,715
Here, take your pick.

376
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:05,290
You've been using that car ever since?

377
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:07,860
What's wrong with that?

378
00:17:10,062 --> 00:17:13,065
Mom said it’s a waste,
with just the three of us.

379
00:17:14,099 --> 00:17:15,267
Did she?

380
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:16,969
And then the argument started.

381
00:17:19,171 --> 00:17:20,272
Do you like that car?

382
00:17:22,474 --> 00:17:24,877
The old commercial they did was awesome.

383
00:17:24,943 --> 00:17:26,512
The husband, wife, kids,

384
00:17:26,578 --> 00:17:29,081
grandparents, even a big dog,

385
00:17:29,148 --> 00:17:30,182
they all go to the beach.

386
00:17:30,249 --> 00:17:32,284
Seeing the whole family goofing around,

387
00:17:32,351 --> 00:17:34,386
the dad just casually
takes off his sunglasses

388
00:17:34,453 --> 00:17:36,155
and goes,

389
00:17:36,655 --> 00:17:38,524
"This is a man’s happiness!

390
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:41,593
A man’s car is this and whatnot."

391
00:17:43,462 --> 00:17:45,531
It was a wonderful ad.

392
00:17:46,331 --> 00:17:47,599
Want something to drink?

393
00:17:48,367 --> 00:17:50,002
I'll have some later.

394
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,036
Okay.

395
00:17:56,708 --> 00:17:58,777
- How about some snacks?
- I said later!

396
00:17:58,844 --> 00:18:00,612
Oh, okay.

397
00:18:03,682 --> 00:18:06,318
Fine, I’ll take the jelly.

398
00:18:07,319 --> 00:18:08,220
Sure.

399
00:18:10,155 --> 00:18:12,858
I like these too.

400
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,596
- Is this fate?
- Huh?

401
00:18:17,663 --> 00:18:19,331
Sorry. Forget what I said.

402
00:18:19,398 --> 00:18:20,532
Here you go.

403
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:22,201
Thanks.

404
00:18:25,471 --> 00:18:27,139
- So, Hatano…
- Yes?

405
00:18:27,806 --> 00:18:29,108
How open are you about it?

406
00:18:29,174 --> 00:18:31,610
You mean, coming out?

407
00:18:31,677 --> 00:18:32,845
Hotaru’s dad

408
00:18:32,911 --> 00:18:34,947
confronted me and asked,

409
00:18:35,013 --> 00:18:36,515
"You swing that way too?"

410
00:18:38,016 --> 00:18:41,019
That’s because he saw us together.
Sorry about that.

411
00:18:41,086 --> 00:18:43,155
Oh, no. I might’ve mentioned this before,

412
00:18:43,222 --> 00:18:45,357
but I don’t really hide it.

413
00:18:45,991 --> 00:18:49,228
I’m a bit careful at school,
since it'd be a hassle.

414
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:52,898
But I was wondering
how you handle it, Hatano.

415
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,802
Personally, my family back home knows,

416
00:18:56,869 --> 00:18:58,270
and my best friend…

417
00:18:58,337 --> 00:19:00,439
- The property agent?
- Yes.

418
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:02,407
And lastly, Hotaru.

419
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:04,243
That's about it.

420
00:19:04,743 --> 00:19:05,677
Well…

421
00:19:06,411 --> 00:19:09,047
If we’re talking about people
I’m close with, that is.

422
00:19:10,115 --> 00:19:12,751
I only tell those I trust.

423
00:19:13,252 --> 00:19:14,086
Okay.

424
00:19:15,954 --> 00:19:16,788
Oh, but Yoshida too.

425
00:19:18,357 --> 00:19:19,525
Along with…

426
00:19:19,591 --> 00:19:23,195
Hotaru's dad. It couldn't be helped.

427
00:19:28,133 --> 00:19:29,401
We’ve got time. Let's check it out.

428
00:19:29,468 --> 00:19:30,502
NO PLANS FOR DISCHARGE

429
00:19:30,569 --> 00:19:32,271
It says no water release today.

430
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:35,641
Why does it have to be him?

431
00:19:35,707 --> 00:19:36,575
Huh?

432
00:19:38,243 --> 00:19:39,244
He's gay, right?

433
00:19:40,779 --> 00:19:42,514
You're one to talk.

434
00:19:45,450 --> 00:19:47,619
I realized I was gay
when I touched his beard.

435
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:48,720
Really?

436
00:19:48,787 --> 00:19:50,455
He was my senior from middle school.

437
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:53,625
When I looked closely,
I noticed he had hair under his chin.

438
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:57,563
It was just a few,
but it was definitely there.

439
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:01,333
When I got to touch it,

440
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,268
strangely, my heart raced like crazy.

441
00:20:05,003 --> 00:20:07,506
That’s when I realized,
"Oh, so this is love."

442
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:12,077
But that senior said he was going
to shave it immediately.

443
00:20:12,144 --> 00:20:13,912
So, before he did, I asked for a strand.

444
00:20:13,979 --> 00:20:14,813
You what?

445
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,848
After that, I would put
that strand by my pillow

446
00:20:16,915 --> 00:20:19,518
when I went to sleep.
I wrapped it in a tissue.

447
00:20:20,152 --> 00:20:23,188
But they thought it was trash
and threw it away.

448
00:20:23,255 --> 00:20:25,724
I was so sad.

449
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:28,293
It was proof of my first love after all.

450
00:20:29,861 --> 00:20:33,398
Of course, I couldn’t confess
to him that I liked him.

451
00:20:33,932 --> 00:20:36,335
For me, that tiny hair

452
00:20:36,835 --> 00:20:39,238
was the only proof that I loved someone.

453
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,141
I cried my eyes out.

454
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:46,311
I drove every adult around me nuts.

455
00:20:48,847 --> 00:20:50,882
When the strand was gone,

456
00:20:51,383 --> 00:20:55,053
it felt like the part of me
that loved him disappeared too.

457
00:20:55,887 --> 00:20:58,357
But if it was gone,

458
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,092
that also means it existed.

459
00:21:01,727 --> 00:21:04,796
That strand of hair did exist.

460
00:21:06,798 --> 00:21:10,669
And so did that love.

461
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:13,438
Yeah.

462
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:17,042
What about you, Hatano? Your first love.

463
00:21:18,710 --> 00:21:21,880
There was this kid in middle school too

464
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,849
that I really liked.

465
00:21:24,883 --> 00:21:26,218
I was the same as you.

466
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,787
Couldn’t confess, of course,

467
00:21:28,854 --> 00:21:31,123
but we got close as friends.

468
00:21:31,189 --> 00:21:34,293
His name is written as "carp"
and "ascend", pronounced as "Koito".

469
00:21:35,027 --> 00:21:36,395
That's a cute name.

470
00:21:36,461 --> 00:21:37,629
I know, right?

471
00:21:38,597 --> 00:21:42,234
We were always together.
In fact, so much so,

472
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:44,603
we were teased by our classmates.

473
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:46,605
"I bet you guys are gay!"

474
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:49,741
I got scared of being found out.

475
00:21:50,242 --> 00:21:51,543
I get how you feel.

476
00:21:52,711 --> 00:21:55,747
So, I joined in and teased Koito about it.

477
00:21:56,248 --> 00:21:57,316
That was how we ended.

478
00:21:58,417 --> 00:21:59,751
Oh…

479
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:02,220
I hurt the person I loved

480
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:04,356
and ran away.

481
00:22:04,423 --> 00:22:07,859
My first love and my best friend…

482
00:22:08,393 --> 00:22:11,196
I lost both at once.

483
00:22:13,865 --> 00:22:16,735
But the fact they’re gone

484
00:22:17,969 --> 00:22:20,138
means they did exist…

485
00:22:23,608 --> 00:22:24,643
At the very least,

486
00:22:24,710 --> 00:22:27,279
that’s what I want to believe.

487
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:33,151
One thing I liked…

488
00:22:33,885 --> 00:22:36,688
There’s a kamidana here.

489
00:22:37,989 --> 00:22:40,359
I never felt lonely,

490
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:42,961
even spending a week alone
in such a big house.

491
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:46,064
I guess it’s because of this.

492
00:22:46,131 --> 00:22:48,066
Well noted.

493
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,769
The house I used to live in had one too.

494
00:22:51,336 --> 00:22:53,872
Every morning,
I’d pray with my grandmother.

495
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:56,041
But when she passed away,

496
00:22:56,108 --> 00:22:58,143
the kamidana was thrown out.

497
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,679
That's the norm these days.

498
00:23:00,746 --> 00:23:01,646
Back then,

499
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:04,182
the security and safety
people used to pray to the gods for

500
00:23:04,249 --> 00:23:06,618
can now be bought with insurance.

501
00:23:08,153 --> 00:23:09,421
It's becoming less common.

502
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,022
Kamidana, that is.

503
00:23:11,523 --> 00:23:14,693
So, they’ll just keep disappearing?

504
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:18,096
Better burn it into my memory while I can.

505
00:23:19,431 --> 00:23:20,599
Let’s do that.

506
00:23:40,919 --> 00:23:41,920
Take this!

507
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:43,422
What do you want?

508
00:23:44,990 --> 00:23:46,691
I'm so sorry!

509
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:48,460
I didn't know you’re with the police.

510
00:23:48,527 --> 00:23:51,696
Good to see you’re security-conscious.

511
00:23:52,297 --> 00:23:53,131
Today, you're here for?

512
00:23:53,198 --> 00:23:56,535
The other day, together
with Hotaru Kusunoki and her dad,

513
00:23:56,601 --> 00:23:58,336
we had a session.

514
00:23:59,004 --> 00:24:00,472
Her dad?

515
00:24:00,539 --> 00:24:03,141
Yes, uh… Mr. Jin Ichigaya.

516
00:24:04,376 --> 00:24:06,578
His stage name is Genichi Hatano?

517
00:24:09,381 --> 00:24:11,650
He said he had pursued
a career as a musician.

518
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:13,952
What is he like?

519
00:24:14,886 --> 00:24:15,987
What do you mean?

520
00:24:17,522 --> 00:24:19,324
He's unusual, isn't he?

521
00:24:19,391 --> 00:24:20,225
Oh, no.

522
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:23,895
He really comes across as a good dad.

523
00:24:23,962 --> 00:24:25,297
Is that right?

524
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:29,801
Oops.

525
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,909
Have you heard him sing?

526
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:39,511
Mr. Hatano’s songs.

527
00:24:40,612 --> 00:24:42,514
Oh, yes.

528
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:44,015
What kind of songs does he sing?

529
00:24:44,082 --> 00:24:46,284
About not having a home,
or something like that.

530
00:24:46,351 --> 00:24:47,352
Does he not have a home?

531
00:24:47,419 --> 00:24:49,321
Uh, well…

532
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:51,289
He does have a home.

533
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:53,692
He lives with Hotaru, after all.

534
00:24:54,292 --> 00:24:55,760
Is it a dark song?

535
00:24:57,229 --> 00:24:58,163
No,

536
00:24:58,230 --> 00:25:00,599
it's more on the passionate side, I’d say.

537
00:25:02,734 --> 00:25:05,203
- I see.
- Is there a problem?

538
00:25:05,270 --> 00:25:07,105
No, I was just curious.

539
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:08,173
Okay.

540
00:25:09,107 --> 00:25:09,941
That's good.

541
00:25:10,909 --> 00:25:11,743
What's good?

542
00:25:12,544 --> 00:25:14,346
Ah, no, it’s nothing.

543
00:25:14,412 --> 00:25:15,480
Really nothing.

544
00:25:15,981 --> 00:25:17,616
Welcome!

545
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:20,986
We'll have two sets of dam curry.

546
00:25:21,052 --> 00:25:22,020
Okay, two sets.

547
00:25:22,087 --> 00:25:23,722
- That'd be 2,000 ye--
- What about Mom's?

548
00:25:24,222 --> 00:25:25,857
- What?
- Mom's portion.

549
00:25:28,493 --> 00:25:30,462
Make it three sets of dam curry.

550
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:32,764
Doesn't it feel nostalgic?

551
00:25:32,831 --> 00:25:34,900
The three of us went out
on drives together.

552
00:25:34,966 --> 00:25:37,502
Until I got carsick, threw up,
and got yelled at.

553
00:25:38,737 --> 00:25:39,671
But oh.

554
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:42,374
The dam release!
It was so impressive that you--

555
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,642
I was so scared, I cried.

556
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:44,743
The dam curry.

557
00:25:44,809 --> 00:25:46,344
You were saying how good it was!

558
00:25:46,411 --> 00:25:49,447
I got grumpy midway
and went back to the car early.

559
00:25:49,514 --> 00:25:52,417
You and Mom ate the leftover curry
and got so stuffed.

560
00:25:54,452 --> 00:25:56,821
Why do you only remember those parts?

561
00:25:58,924 --> 00:26:00,859
What about today? Are you having fun?

562
00:26:02,594 --> 00:26:03,995
Were you trying to make it fun?

563
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:05,897
I'm better, right?

564
00:26:12,170 --> 00:26:14,906
I handle things like a dad better, right?

565
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,909
I thought you didn’t
want to take care of me.

566
00:26:19,077 --> 00:26:20,045
You're right.

567
00:26:20,111 --> 00:26:21,346
So, why?

568
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,014
I don’t get you, seriously.

569
00:26:23,915 --> 00:26:27,519
But if I don’t do better than him,

570
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,354
I would lose, and that's just not right.

571
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,989
What are you competing for?

572
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:36,761
You’ve got a new family now,

573
00:26:36,828 --> 00:26:38,863
so just go and be their dad.

574
00:26:40,799 --> 00:26:43,168
That’s long gone.

575
00:26:44,069 --> 00:26:45,503
We divorced.

576
00:26:45,570 --> 00:26:48,406
I lost everything and am totally broke.

577
00:26:52,510 --> 00:26:53,745
What an idiot.

578
00:26:56,047 --> 00:26:57,482
You’re the idiot here!

579
00:26:58,149 --> 00:26:59,985
I'm the one who wrote that letter.

580
00:27:01,820 --> 00:27:03,989
Sorry for the wait!

581
00:27:07,192 --> 00:27:09,227
Just hand it over!

582
00:27:16,768 --> 00:27:19,638
DAM CURRY

583
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:26,277
What the hell are you doing here?

584
00:27:26,344 --> 00:27:27,712
Please give that back!

585
00:27:27,779 --> 00:27:28,713
It’s not yours!

586
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:30,048
It’s hers!

587
00:27:30,548 --> 00:27:31,916
Even the teacher is here?

588
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:33,585
Stop giving me more work!

589
00:27:33,652 --> 00:27:35,086
Let go!

590
00:27:35,153 --> 00:27:36,454
Sakuta!

591
00:27:36,521 --> 00:27:38,023
Please give us three sets of dam curry!

592
00:27:38,089 --> 00:27:39,124
Three? Got it.

593
00:27:39,190 --> 00:27:41,693
- I'm hungry!
- I know, since we walked a lot!

594
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:44,195
- I can't wait to eat!
- You're really hungry, huh?

595
00:27:44,262 --> 00:27:45,930
You love curry.

596
00:27:45,997 --> 00:27:47,365
Dam curry for everyone!

597
00:27:47,432 --> 00:27:48,500
Where are you running to?

598
00:27:50,268 --> 00:27:51,369
A slope?

599
00:27:59,110 --> 00:28:00,245
Wait!

600
00:28:06,051 --> 00:28:07,118
Let go of me!

601
00:28:09,688 --> 00:28:10,555
Got it!

602
00:28:13,425 --> 00:28:15,593
- This is my money!
- You're wrong.

603
00:28:16,561 --> 00:28:18,129
It's embezzled money!

604
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:20,999
Which means it’s not yours either!

605
00:28:21,499 --> 00:28:24,269
Hey, Sakuta! Saku-- Huh?

606
00:28:25,937 --> 00:28:26,838
What's going on?

607
00:28:26,905 --> 00:28:28,640
- Dang it!
- That letter

608
00:28:28,707 --> 00:28:30,642
was written by you, wasn't it?

609
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:31,810
Such a horrible lie!

610
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:35,714
You lied too, saying the money
was not with you!

611
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:38,783
Are you really that desperate for money?

612
00:28:38,850 --> 00:28:40,285
I’m going to start all over!

613
00:28:40,351 --> 00:28:41,252
What?

614
00:28:41,853 --> 00:28:43,321
A completely different life!

615
00:28:43,822 --> 00:28:45,023
What do you mean by that?

616
00:28:45,090 --> 00:28:46,391
Different means different, duh!

617
00:28:46,458 --> 00:28:47,559
Huh?

618
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:49,994
Anyway, just different, you idiot!

619
00:28:50,829 --> 00:28:53,131
- I don’t understand what you’re saying!
- Damn it!

620
00:28:54,632 --> 00:28:56,000
What does a gay guy even know?

621
00:28:58,837 --> 00:29:00,572
You can’t even have kids!

622
00:29:02,540 --> 00:29:05,577
Why would Hotaru want someone like you?

623
00:29:05,643 --> 00:29:07,445
Why does she want a gay guy?

624
00:29:07,512 --> 00:29:08,913
Meanwhile, I'm normal.

625
00:29:09,848 --> 00:29:11,316
And she's my daughter!

626
00:29:12,383 --> 00:29:15,420
And yet I can’t even be a proper dad!

627
00:29:15,487 --> 00:29:17,255
Why can’t I be a man?

628
00:29:17,322 --> 00:29:18,623
It's always like this! Always!

629
00:29:20,725 --> 00:29:22,227
- What, got a problem?
- No.

630
00:29:22,293 --> 00:29:23,027
What is it?

631
00:29:24,062 --> 00:29:25,163
What's your deal? Move it!

632
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,266
Sakuta!

633
00:29:30,802 --> 00:29:32,470
Okay, nicely done.

634
00:29:41,479 --> 00:29:42,347
Oh, come on!

635
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,256
Sakuta!

636
00:29:51,990 --> 00:29:54,926
Sorry, but I'm leaving the rest to you!

637
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:56,427
W… Wait…

638
00:30:00,031 --> 00:30:01,366
This can't be happening…

639
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:03,334
It's coming. Just wait.

640
00:30:03,401 --> 00:30:06,604
- Here you go. Sorry for the wait!
- It's here.

641
00:30:06,671 --> 00:30:08,306
This is the dam curry.

642
00:30:08,373 --> 00:30:10,542
- It really does look like a dam.
- It looks yummy!

643
00:30:10,608 --> 00:30:12,477
- Wow!
- Thank you.

644
00:30:12,544 --> 00:30:13,778
Kusunoki…

645
00:30:14,512 --> 00:30:15,713
Hotaru!

646
00:30:16,214 --> 00:30:17,348
Mr. Sakuta.

647
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:22,086
- Why are you here?
- I came with your dad.

648
00:30:23,721 --> 00:30:25,824
Hatano, I meant.

649
00:30:25,890 --> 00:30:26,791
Uh-huh.

650
00:30:28,259 --> 00:30:29,294
Um…

651
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:33,398
- Your mom…
- She won't be coming, right?

652
00:30:33,898 --> 00:30:34,732
I know.

653
00:30:39,103 --> 00:30:40,271
You may eat it.

654
00:30:42,874 --> 00:30:44,175
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

655
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,414
Here.

656
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:56,654
- I'm digging in.
- Likewise.

657
00:30:57,789 --> 00:30:59,858
Let's dig in!

658
00:31:02,493 --> 00:31:04,195
Oh, it's so cool!

659
00:31:04,262 --> 00:31:05,930
- It really is!
- Wow.

660
00:31:05,997 --> 00:31:07,198
Amazing!

661
00:31:07,966 --> 00:31:10,335
- That's a big piece.
- Can you eat it?

662
00:31:10,401 --> 00:31:12,704
Am I… eating this the right way?

663
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:22,680
He’s a terrible dad.

664
00:31:26,651 --> 00:31:28,653
There are so many bad memories.

665
00:31:31,422 --> 00:31:34,158
But there were also memorable ones.

666
00:31:41,266 --> 00:31:42,934
They’re all gone now.

667
00:31:44,335 --> 00:31:46,271
I can't even get to see Mom.

668
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:51,276
Everything’s gone.

669
00:31:55,947 --> 00:31:57,916
If it’s gone…

670
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:01,586
that means it once existed.

671
00:32:04,255 --> 00:32:05,356
Well…

672
00:32:06,457 --> 00:32:08,192
That's what Hatano said.

673
00:32:12,163 --> 00:32:13,097
Right.

674
00:32:32,517 --> 00:32:35,620
Thank you for today.

675
00:32:35,687 --> 00:32:36,587
Don't worry about it.

676
00:32:36,654 --> 00:32:38,389
I got this in return, so…

677
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,558
You’re really kind.

678
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,160
You're giving me too much credit.

679
00:32:42,226 --> 00:32:43,428
Thank you.

680
00:32:43,494 --> 00:32:46,631
Honestly, it’s just that reporting you
to the police would be a huge hassle.

681
00:32:46,698 --> 00:32:49,901
Besides, I find backpackers
kinda interesting.

682
00:32:51,536 --> 00:32:54,706
For a long time,
I couldn’t really go anywhere.

683
00:32:54,772 --> 00:32:56,140
I was living in Tokyo,

684
00:32:56,207 --> 00:32:59,477
and I'd just go see the nearby dam.
I've been living that kind of life.

685
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:02,480
And, well, it was fine, but…

686
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,552
Never mind. Forget what I said.

687
00:33:07,618 --> 00:33:08,786
Enjoy yourself.

688
00:33:08,853 --> 00:33:10,555
And good luck finding a place to stay!

689
00:33:11,289 --> 00:33:13,091
- Thank you.
- Well then.

690
00:33:20,365 --> 00:33:21,199
Thank you for having me.

691
00:33:21,265 --> 00:33:22,166
No, not at all.

692
00:33:22,233 --> 00:33:24,202
- I’ll come again.
- To listen to his songs?

693
00:33:24,268 --> 00:33:25,136
Yes.

694
00:33:25,870 --> 00:33:27,939
No, to check on things.

695
00:33:28,573 --> 00:33:29,674
See you.

696
00:33:30,174 --> 00:33:31,309
I'll take my leave.

697
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,448
Are you sure I can
have them all to myself?

698
00:33:38,683 --> 00:33:40,018
Yeah, no need to hesitate.

699
00:33:45,456 --> 00:33:46,758
Where's my dad?

700
00:33:48,459 --> 00:33:49,627
Which one?

701
00:33:51,462 --> 00:33:52,930
Both.

702
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:54,899
I spilled a bit.

703
00:33:55,900 --> 00:33:57,201
It's fine.

704
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:59,170
Sorry.

705
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:03,908
You good for the restroom?
Need me to stop at a roadside station?

706
00:34:04,409 --> 00:34:05,877
I'm good.

707
00:34:06,844 --> 00:34:10,314
You can't do this. I said no.

708
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:12,984
Ouch! You're hurting me!

709
00:34:13,051 --> 00:34:14,886
What are you doing?

710
00:34:17,255 --> 00:34:18,289
Damn it!

711
00:34:32,203 --> 00:34:33,037
‪INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

712
00:34:36,908 --> 00:34:38,242
Were you okay?

713
00:34:40,611 --> 00:34:42,113
Where's Hatano?

714
00:34:42,180 --> 00:34:43,781
He went to retrieve the suitcase.

715
00:34:43,848 --> 00:34:45,083
He left the rest to me, he said.

716
00:34:45,149 --> 00:34:46,818
What? Will he be okay?

717
00:34:47,985 --> 00:34:49,053
He really didn't have to go

718
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:51,189
that far for just a suitcase.

719
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:55,860
Wait, what did you just say?

720
00:34:57,728 --> 00:34:58,563
Huh?

721
00:35:01,999 --> 00:35:03,401
Hey!

722
00:35:04,435 --> 00:35:05,369
- Hey, um…
- Sorry.

723
00:35:05,436 --> 00:35:07,438
What… Come on!

724
00:35:07,505 --> 00:35:08,606
I'm really sorry, but…

725
00:35:08,673 --> 00:35:09,907
- Will you get off?
- No, sorry.

726
00:35:09,974 --> 00:35:12,043
Hey!

727
00:35:12,577 --> 00:35:13,411
- Get off--
- No.

728
00:35:14,045 --> 00:35:14,879
The money…

729
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:17,048
What are you going to do with it?

730
00:35:18,382 --> 00:35:19,417
What?

731
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:22,520
What do you want?

732
00:35:24,555 --> 00:35:25,389
A house, maybe?

733
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:26,390
Why a house?

734
00:35:26,457 --> 00:35:27,592
Buying a house

735
00:35:28,292 --> 00:35:30,461
and using it as a "clamp"
is my personal goal.

736
00:35:31,028 --> 00:35:32,730
A "clamp"?

737
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:36,200
That's "love and revolution".

738
00:35:36,267 --> 00:35:37,768
You're creeping me out.

739
00:35:38,736 --> 00:35:39,704
Huh?

740
00:35:41,272 --> 00:35:43,574
Are you sure we can just enter?

741
00:35:43,641 --> 00:35:44,809
Yeah.

742
00:35:45,877 --> 00:35:46,844
It should be fine.

743
00:35:48,579 --> 00:35:50,214
Please excuse me.

744
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:05,296
We're already in Tokyo!
Just get off already!

745
00:36:05,363 --> 00:36:06,631
Never!

746
00:36:06,697 --> 00:36:08,499
Not until I bring this back with me.

747
00:36:08,566 --> 00:36:10,368
This is something precious to her!

748
00:36:14,906 --> 00:36:15,840
What?

749
00:36:15,907 --> 00:36:16,941
Huh?

750
00:36:18,976 --> 00:36:20,311
So, you knew?

751
00:36:20,378 --> 00:36:23,181
The letter wasn’t from your mom.

752
00:36:23,247 --> 00:36:25,082
It doesn’t even look like her handwriting.

753
00:36:25,816 --> 00:36:28,953
I wonder who’s really the idiot here.

754
00:36:29,687 --> 00:36:31,689
But you went anyway.

755
00:36:31,756 --> 00:36:33,658
I just thought about thinking positively.

756
00:36:34,225 --> 00:36:35,326
Thinking positively?

757
00:36:35,393 --> 00:36:36,994
Maybe,

758
00:36:37,061 --> 00:36:38,529
just maybe,

759
00:36:38,596 --> 00:36:40,398
Mom will come.

760
00:36:40,464 --> 00:36:41,799
Maybe I’ll get to see her.

761
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:43,034
So, that's how it is.

762
00:36:43,100 --> 00:36:43,935
Yeah.

763
00:36:51,142 --> 00:36:52,310
Do you wanna go for a walk?

764
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:55,179
Did it not get to go out for a walk?

765
00:36:55,780 --> 00:36:57,548
Probably…

766
00:37:17,134 --> 00:37:18,502
You did it because you were asked to?

767
00:37:19,503 --> 00:37:20,805
Yes.

768
00:37:20,871 --> 00:37:21,906
To act as her parent?

769
00:37:21,973 --> 00:37:23,708
You must have a screw loose.

770
00:37:23,774 --> 00:37:25,843
I just want to do what I can right now.

771
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:27,478
Huh?

772
00:37:29,146 --> 00:37:30,281
You said

773
00:37:30,348 --> 00:37:32,283
you can't be a proper dad.

774
00:37:33,117 --> 00:37:36,187
Well, I’ve got a lot I can’t do too.

775
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:38,689
To begin with, I’ve failed at more things

776
00:37:38,756 --> 00:37:41,125
than most people. That's what I feel.

777
00:37:42,026 --> 00:37:45,296
So, all I can do is what I'm able
to do every day.

778
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:48,532
And what do you know?

779
00:37:49,033 --> 00:37:51,802
Things somehow turn out alright.

780
00:37:53,004 --> 00:37:54,338
How so?

781
00:37:54,405 --> 00:37:55,239
How should I put it?

782
00:37:56,040 --> 00:37:57,208
It's like being alive…

783
00:37:58,542 --> 00:37:59,744
feels good.

784
00:38:00,845 --> 00:38:01,679
What are the things

785
00:38:02,246 --> 00:38:03,314
you're able to do?

786
00:38:04,915 --> 00:38:06,517
Like walking the dog every day.

787
00:38:06,584 --> 00:38:08,052
Do they perhaps remember the route?

788
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:09,687
- Hello!
- Hello!

789
00:38:09,754 --> 00:38:10,621
Smiling and greeting.

790
00:38:10,688 --> 00:38:11,589
Hello.

791
00:38:11,656 --> 00:38:14,392
- The dogs are so cute!
- Go ahead.

792
00:38:14,458 --> 00:38:16,627
Giving way to others.

793
00:38:20,164 --> 00:38:21,098
A grasshopper.

794
00:38:22,066 --> 00:38:23,834
Releasing a bug back into the wild.

795
00:38:24,902 --> 00:38:26,704
Huh? A bug?

796
00:38:26,771 --> 00:38:29,173
It doesn’t have to be anything big.

797
00:38:29,674 --> 00:38:31,108
Just stick to what you can handle.

798
00:38:31,175 --> 00:38:33,811
I recommend it. Little by little,
that’s how you do it.

799
00:38:33,878 --> 00:38:34,979
What?

800
00:38:35,046 --> 00:38:36,380
Everyone has their own

801
00:38:37,048 --> 00:38:38,449
"love and revolution", I guess.

802
00:38:39,550 --> 00:38:41,018
What does that even mean?

803
00:38:44,288 --> 00:38:45,956
Even for a person like me,

804
00:38:47,425 --> 00:38:48,592
is there anything I can do?

805
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:50,494
Of course!

806
00:38:50,561 --> 00:38:51,962
Will being alive

807
00:38:53,130 --> 00:38:53,964
feel good?

808
00:38:54,632 --> 00:38:56,667
Yeah, totally!

809
00:39:00,137 --> 00:39:01,706
Don’t make it sound so easy!

810
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:09,947
Ah, wait… Hey!

811
00:39:25,429 --> 00:39:26,564
Hello!

812
00:39:30,601 --> 00:39:32,069
Okay, here.

813
00:39:32,903 --> 00:39:34,638
Here you go.

814
00:39:35,473 --> 00:39:38,008
- This is a souvenir from my business trip.
- Thank you.

815
00:39:39,009 --> 00:39:41,178
I got this as a gift,
but share it with Genichi.

816
00:39:42,279 --> 00:39:45,015
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

817
00:39:45,082 --> 00:39:46,250
Welcome back!

818
00:39:46,751 --> 00:39:49,053
- Welcome back!
- I'm back.

819
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:49,987
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

820
00:39:50,054 --> 00:39:51,021
You walked the dogs?

821
00:39:51,088 --> 00:39:52,456
They asked us to.

822
00:39:52,523 --> 00:39:53,858
Thanks.

823
00:39:53,924 --> 00:39:55,292
He returned the suitcase?

824
00:39:55,359 --> 00:39:56,494
Look,

825
00:39:57,161 --> 00:39:59,697
could you please let me know
what's inside beforehand?

826
00:39:59,764 --> 00:40:01,332
It was exhausting.

827
00:40:02,133 --> 00:40:04,468
That's why I said I'm taking the suitcase.

828
00:40:05,035 --> 00:40:06,203
Didn't I?

829
00:40:06,270 --> 00:40:07,671
Is that what you meant?

830
00:40:08,672 --> 00:40:10,408
How'd you expect me to get it?

831
00:40:13,010 --> 00:40:14,578
Sorry you had to take them out.

832
00:40:14,645 --> 00:40:15,980
Oh, it's okay.

833
00:40:18,716 --> 00:40:20,518
There's a grasshopper on your foot.

834
00:40:23,220 --> 00:40:24,922
It must've followed me from earlier.

835
00:40:24,989 --> 00:40:25,923
What?

836
00:40:25,990 --> 00:40:28,626
It was about to get stepped on,
so I let it back into the grass.

837
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:34,665
You have a grasshopper on you too.

838
00:40:41,338 --> 00:40:42,807
Isn't this fate?

839
00:40:46,377 --> 00:40:48,078
Yeah, it's fate.

840
00:40:50,314 --> 00:40:51,215
Huh?

841
00:40:53,417 --> 00:40:54,785
What did you just say?

842
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:01,492
DRIED SALMON

843
00:41:01,559 --> 00:41:03,961
Okay, over here.

844
00:41:04,662 --> 00:41:05,863
Please write your name.

845
00:41:09,867 --> 00:41:12,536
- Do I have to?
- Yes.

846
00:41:14,371 --> 00:41:15,306
Okay.

847
00:41:17,741 --> 00:41:18,609
SAKU SAKUTA

848
00:41:18,676 --> 00:41:22,213
Oh, by the way, I asked the landlord,

849
00:41:22,279 --> 00:41:23,514
and I borrowed an empty unit.

850
00:41:23,581 --> 00:41:25,115
- What?
- Really?

851
00:41:25,182 --> 00:41:26,784
Until I find a new place to move.

852
00:41:26,851 --> 00:41:28,185
Please treat me well.

853
00:41:33,357 --> 00:41:34,191
Okay!

854
00:41:34,258 --> 00:41:39,597
PARTY C - SAKU SAKUTA

855
00:41:41,932 --> 00:41:44,735
The garden shovel

856
00:41:44,802 --> 00:41:47,404
Was wet all day

857
00:41:47,972 --> 00:41:51,108
Then the rain stopped

858
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:54,278
And I sneezed

859
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:56,247
After the beep tone,

860
00:41:56,313 --> 00:41:59,049
please leave your name and message.

861
00:41:59,116 --> 00:42:00,985
Hello, Mom?

862
00:42:01,051 --> 00:42:02,319
Hey, Mom.

863
00:42:02,386 --> 00:42:04,321
Remember that time the three of us
went to the dam?

864
00:42:04,388 --> 00:42:05,189
NO PLANS FOR DISCHARGE

865
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:06,690
On the way back, in the car,

866
00:42:06,757 --> 00:42:09,126
we all sang at the top of our lungs.

867
00:42:09,727 --> 00:42:11,495
I can’t remember what song it was,

868
00:42:11,562 --> 00:42:13,964
but I had so much fun.

869
00:42:15,332 --> 00:42:19,169
We’ll probably never
go out together like that…

870
00:42:19,236 --> 00:42:19,837
DAM CURRY

871
00:42:19,904 --> 00:42:22,006
…never eat curry together,
or sing like that ever again.

872
00:42:22,072 --> 00:42:24,808
But that timeline… It really existed.

873
00:42:26,010 --> 00:42:28,712
Someday, tell me more
about your memories, Mom.

874
00:42:29,313 --> 00:42:30,648
Talk to you soon.

875
00:42:36,420 --> 00:42:39,390
The fresh laundry…

876
00:42:39,456 --> 00:42:40,324
Thank you.

877
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:43,994
If you came all this way,
you must've not found a house yet.

878
00:42:44,061 --> 00:42:45,262
I think it'll be soon.

879
00:42:45,329 --> 00:42:46,697
Oh yeah?

880
00:42:46,764 --> 00:42:48,265
I thought maybe
you had lingering feelings.

881
00:42:48,933 --> 00:42:51,902
- No, not at all.
- Really?

882
00:42:55,339 --> 00:42:57,775
- Yeah, nope.
- A bit cold, huh?

883
00:42:58,943 --> 00:43:01,111
La la la

884
00:43:01,178 --> 00:43:03,981
A rainbow, a rainbow

885
00:43:04,048 --> 00:43:06,784
Stretched across the sky

886
00:43:06,850 --> 00:43:09,520
And your, your

887
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:12,389
Mood cleared up too

888
00:43:12,456 --> 00:43:15,392
Surely tomorrow

889
00:43:15,459 --> 00:43:18,162
Will be a clear sky

890
00:43:18,228 --> 00:43:21,131
Surely tomorrow

891
00:43:21,198 --> 00:43:24,568
Will be a clear sky

892
00:43:25,970 --> 00:43:28,172
Nacchi!

893
00:43:28,238 --> 00:43:29,340
Hey, what's up?

894
00:43:29,406 --> 00:43:30,741
Hey, Nacchi.

895
00:43:33,010 --> 00:43:34,278
- What are you doing?
- She's crazy.

896
00:43:34,345 --> 00:43:35,379
I'm studying.

897
00:43:35,446 --> 00:43:36,280
What?

898
00:43:36,847 --> 00:43:38,549
Koinobori!

899
00:43:38,616 --> 00:43:39,683
- One plus one?
- How do I solve this?

900
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:41,218
- Which one?
- What's two plus…

901
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:42,319
- This.
- Make yourself at home.

902
00:43:42,386 --> 00:43:44,154
- Okay.
- You can sit wherever.

903
00:43:44,221 --> 00:43:45,556
- Got it.
- Thanks.

904
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:48,759
INOKASHIRA

905
00:43:52,363 --> 00:43:53,430
TO KYOKO INOKASHIRA

906
00:43:53,497 --> 00:43:55,966
FROM TOMOE KUSUNOKI

907
00:45:52,049 --> 00:45:54,017
Subtitle translation by: Jeffery
